#order CHANGELOG.md
#order README.md
#order docs/installation.md
#order .github/release.yml
#order .github/CODEOWNERS
#reason .github/CODEOWNERS Makes the maintainer the default reviewer of every path in the public repository.
#reason .github/release.yml Gives generated GitHub release notes readable categories instead of one flat list.
#reason CHANGELOG.md Gives readers a record of what each release contains, starting with 0.2.0.
#reason README.md Shows project status at a glance and tells visitors where to download Lantern.
#reason docs/installation.md Puts the download route and its signing caveats next to the build-from-source steps.
#story A visitor downloads Lantern
#step actor A visitor
#file README.md
#step action opens the repository page
#file README.md
#step subject the README
#file README.md
#file docs/installation.md
#below interaction Finds badges and a Download section with the releases link
#below consequence No download guidance => Packages and signing notes are explained
#story A maintainer publishes a release
#step actor A maintainer
#file CHANGELOG.md
#step action publishes a release
#file .github/release.yml
#step subject the release notes
#file .github/release.yml
#file .github/CODEOWNERS
#below interaction Gets categorised notes and a changelog to follow
#below consequence One flat list of pull requests => Notes grouped by label
